# Endings: checked in this order on arrival day; the last one has no conditions.
# Each ending is one carrier clause (answered or logged) times one arrival clause
# (held the plan into the storm, waited it out in orbit, or no storm). The core
# truth is the same in all six; see STORY_BIBLE.md.

card end_lights
type ending
cat ending
when flag signal_answered
when flag arrive_hold
text Lights On. The fleet holds the plan and goes down into the storm. At four kilometers the radar fills with sand and the altimeters stop agreeing. Then Cargo 2, awake since their hail landed between boots, turns on every light it has and leaves them on. Seven ships land on it.

card end_through
type ending
cat ending
when flag arrive_hold
text Through the Dust. The fleet holds the plan and goes down into the storm, radar full of sand. At two kilometers one altimeter drops out, and the ships fly on the other two, the way they were built to. Out of the brown, every eleven seconds, a light. Seven ships land on it.

card end_long_orbit
type ending
cat ending
when flag signal_answered
when flag arrive_wait
text The Long Orbit. Four nights of ration math, waiting out the dust. Every pass, Cargo 2 sends a little more of its manifest, slowly, in a format nobody has used in years, and the fleet reads it aloud like letters from home. When the sky clears, seven ships go down to collect.

card end_patience
type ending
cat ending
when flag arrive_wait
text Patience. The fleet waits out the storm in a long orbit: four nights of ration math and half portions, and nobody complains out loud. Every night, through the dust, one point of light keeps time at the edge of the landing zone. When the sky clears, seven ships go down to meet it.

card end_friend
type ending
cat ending
when flag signal_answered
text Old Friend. On final approach the fleet hails it once more on the old channel, between boots. The lights blink, and then hold steady. On the next pass Cargo 2 sends its whole manifest, slowly, in a format nobody has used in years, like something that has been rehearsing.

card end_long_way
type ending
cat ending
text The Long Way Round. Seven ships land in clear air. Afterwards they walk to Cargo 2 in their suits, past its long shadow, and open the hold. The first crate has Sharpie on it, in a hand they know: "You'll thank me." They say it out loud, one at a time, into a hold that has been dark for years.
